infographic compare-binary-horizontal-underline-text-vs
data
  title Metastability: one system, two stable states
  desc Same code, same load shape — the feedback loop decides which equilibrium the system rests in
  compares
    - label Healthy equilibrium
      children
        - label Healthy state
          desc Where the system rests under normal load
        - label Short queue, drains fast
          desc Backlog clears faster than work arrives
        - label Fast responses, few retries
          desc Calls return in ~40ms; recovery is a trickle
        - label Holds with no intervention
          desc No active effort needed to stay here
    - label Collapsed equilibrium
      children
        - label Collapsed state
          desc Where a big enough shock pushes the system
        - label Full queue, self-refilling
          desc Retries refill it faster than it drains
        - label Slow responses, retry storm
          desc Timeouts at 4s; recovery becomes the load
        - label Survives provider recovery
          desc Fixing the trigger does not free the loop
theme
  palette #10b981 #f43f5e
